- op: discuss  # f6dd
  at: '2026-08-02T19:08:23Z'  # f6dd
  by: agent  # f6dd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f6dd
  clock: 5  # f6dd
  nonce: f6dd  # f6dd
  message: "FIXED and merged, PR #167, dev c539caf0b7.\n\npoll_ci now asks whether a status context EXISTS for the SHA rather than whether\none has gone NON-pending. any_job_started -> run_dispatched. A parse failure\nkeeps polling instead of fabricating a hung verdict. CI_STALE_PENDING_SECONDS\ndeliberately unchanged.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (production-path test, not a proxy).\ntests/test_ci_verdict_default_deny.py drives the REAL poll_ci - the library is\nsourced and api_get is overridden in the same shell - against the payload shape\nWoodpecker actually produces. Recorded live during development:\n  BEFORE: one pending aggregate context, threshold elapsed -> RC=3   (the bug)\n  AFTER : same input                                       -> RC=2   (times out normally)\n  AFTER : empty status list, threshold elapsed             -> RC=3   (preserved)\nThat third case is load-bearing: without it the fix would be indistinguishable\nfrom deleting the check. Mutation-tested - restoring the old non-pending\npredicate turns exactly test_a_pending_aggregate_context_is_not_a_hung_runner\nred.\n\nPRODUCTION CORROBORATION OF THE PREMISE, from PR #167's own poll trace:\n    [0s]  (no jobs yet)\n    [10s] waiting: ci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker\n    .........\n    CI Passed!\nExactly ONE context, named as predicted, present within 10s of dispatch and\npending until the pipeline ended. That is the fact the old predicate could never\nsatisfy, observed rather than assumed.\n\nNOT OBSERVED, stated plainly. No CI run since the fix has crossed the 300s\nthreshold - PR #167 completed in ~110s (its manifest is the root suite: 82 files,\n1466 passed, 2 skipped in 11.8s), so the stale-pending branch did not execute in\nproduction. The CHANGED VERDICT is proven by production-path test; the threshold\ncrossing itself has not recurred since the fix landed. A future pipeline over\n300s that merges normally would be the last piece of confirmation, and its\nabsence is why this note says \"test-proven\" rather than \"field-proven\".\n\nRETIRES the explanations this item's INV-rahib Surface 2 lineage had accumulated:\nnot runner contention, not a competing nightly, not shared-volume latency."  # f6dd
